  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Optimisation and sustainabilisation of ASA (aquaculture) in Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dutch company Africa Sustainable Aquaculture (ASA) invested in the set-up of the first sustainable and commercial large-scale fish farm in Ethiopia.Through a DGGF-loan ASA is currently developing its aquaculture activities further. To strengthen the business case, to improve production capacity and to reduce the risks of the investments, Technical Assistance (DGGF-TA) is provided. The TA involves 1) setting-up of a research programme to improve fish quality, fish feed and the production process, 2) developing an export strategy to limit financial risks involved with foreign currency barriers in Ethiopia and 3) preparing for ASC-Certification of the facility to meet European standards and requirements for exports.The project is currently ongoing and expects to provide sustainable knowledge transfer by training 20 employees of the farm for certification. The results of the TA in Ethiopia will serve as a benchmark for further sustainable aquaculture development in East Africa.</narrative>
  </description>
